{"type":"text","timestamp":1794046782424,"sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","part":{"id":"prt_1b5851fff0016riI0ZbEsAStih","messageID":"msg_1b58466d6001w0eijVjMaGw7ry","sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the reviewer-identified DST wall-clock arithmetic bug in `ledgerkit/slots.py` by normalizing all interval math to UTC, add two regression tests, run the tests, and commit to `crew/1107-b2704c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c`; branch: `crew/1107-b2704c`; Python: 3.12.3.\n- Do not push or switch branches.\n- Verified pre-fix bug: `datetime(2025,11,3,0,0,tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York')) - datetime(2025,11,2,0,0,tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))` returns `1 day, 0:00:00` (24 h), not the real 25 h; `free_slots([], ds, de, min_minutes=24*60+30)` returned `[]`.\n- Empirically, Python 3.12.3 aware-datetime subtraction is wall-clock and ignores UTC offsets; aware comparison is instant-based. The fix avoids local-zone subtraction by doing interval math in UTC.\n- Prescribed fix: convert `day_start`, `day_end`, and busy endpoints via `.astimezone(timezone.utc)`; clip, sort, merge, compute gaps, and apply the `min_seconds` filter entirely in UTC; convert returned gap endpoints back via `.astimezone(day_start.tzinfo)`.\n- `busy` is a list of timezone-aware `(start, end)` tuples; intervals may be unsorted, overlapping, or use mixed offsets.\n- Zero-length busy intervals are silently ignored.\n- `ValueError` is required for naive datetimes, any busy interval with `end < start`, and `day_end <= day_start`.\n- Original implementation and 22 tests were committed as `0a201aa`; expected final test count after adding two tests: `24 passed`.\n- Repo root currently shows no `pyproject.toml`, setup file, or lint/typecheck config; visible entries are `.git`, `.gitignore`, `.pytest_cache`, `README.md`, `ledgerkit`, and `tests`.\n- Test assertions for total free time must compute durations in UTC to avoid wall-clock subtraction on returned local-zone datetimes, e.g. `sum(e.astimezone(timezone.utc) - s.astimezone(timezone.utc) for s, e in gaps)`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Original `ledgerkit/slots.py` and `tests/test_slots.py` created, tested, and committed as `0a201aa`.\n- Empirically reproduced the DST bug before fixing it.\n- Rewrote `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/slots.py` with UTC-normalized `free_slots`:\n  - `UTC = timezone.utc`\n  - validation via `_is_naive`\n  - `day_start`/`day_end` converted to UTC\n  - busy endpoints clipped to UTC window\n  - sort/merge/gap calculation performed in UTC\n  - returned endpoints converted back to `day_start.tzinfo`\n- Checked repository layout and confirmed no obvious lint/typecheck configuration.\n\n### Active\n- Add two DST regression tests to `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py`:\n  - `test_fall_back_day_full_window_survives_min_minutes`:\n    - NY window `2025-11-02 00:00` to `2025-11-03 00:00`\n    - `free_slots([], day_start, day_end, min_minutes=24 * 60 + 30)`\n    - expected result `[(day_start, day_end)]`\n  - `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`:\n    - same NY window\n    - busy interval `2025-11-02 01:30` to `01:45` EDT using `timezone(timedelta(hours=-4))`\n    - expected two gaps:\n      - `day_start` to `2025-11-02 01:45 EDT`\n      - `2025-11-02 01:45 EDT` to `day_end`\n    - total UTC duration should be `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=15)`\n- Ensure `tests/test_slots.py` imports `from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo` alongside existing `datetime`, `timedelta`, and `timezone` imports.\n- Run the test suite and commit if green.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Edit `tests/test_slots.py` to add `from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo` and append the two planned DST regression tests, wrapping the total-duration sum for 79-column style.\n2. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` in `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c` and confirm the expected result, `24 passed`.\n3. If tests pass, `git add ledgerkit/slots.py tests/test_slots.py`, commit on `crew/1107-b2704c` with a message such as `Fix DST wall-clock arithmetic by doing interval math in UTC`, and do not push.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/slots.py`: rewritten with UTC-normalized `free_slots` and `_is_naive`; not yet validated by tests or committed.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py`: contains the existing 22 tests; needs two DST regression tests and a `ZoneInfo` import.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing package module, unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_money.py`: existing tests, unchanged.","time":{"start":1794046763007,"end":1794046782420}}}
