{"type":"text","timestamp":1794046933606,"sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","part":{"id":"prt_1b587aa580016DW5aD5hnPrZpY","messageID":"msg_1b585b5f7001Vv2p82ota6hyqs","sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe returned endpoint is 01:30 with `fold=1` (i.e., 06:30 UTC), not the 05:30 UTC I was expecting. I'll check how CPython's `astimezone` handles ambiguous local times in the repeated one-hour window.\n\n","time":{"start":1794046929496,"end":1794046933604}}}
