{"type":"text","timestamp":1794047181275,"sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","part":{"id":"prt_1b58b2765001J6fqESBiM2YrWY","messageID":"msg_1b589da0a001A4g83vhymUewoi","sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the DST wall-clock arithmetic bug in `ledgerkit/slots.py` by normalizing all interval math to UTC, add two regression tests, run the tests green, and commit to `crew/1107-b2704c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c`; branch: `crew/1107-b2704c`; Python: 3.12.3.\n- Do not push or switch branches.\n- Original implementation and 22 tests committed as `0a201aa`; expected final test count after adding two tests: `24 passed`.\n- `free_slots(busy, day_start, day_end, min_minutes=0)` should return sorted, timezone-aware gaps in `day_start`’s timezone, with all interval math (clip, sort, merge, gaps, durations) done in UTC.\n- `busy` is a list of timezone-aware `(start, end)` tuples; intervals may be unsorted, overlapping, or use mixed offsets. Zero-length busy intervals are silently ignored.\n- `ValueError` required for naive datetimes, any busy interval with `end < start`, and `day_end <= day_start`.\n- Test assertions for total free time must compute durations in UTC: `sum(e.astimezone(timezone.utc) - s.astimezone(timezone.utc) for s, e in gaps)`.\n- CPython `astimezone` diagnostic confirmed correct behavior for `America/New_York` fall-back on 2025-11-02:\n  - `05:30 UTC` → `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:30 UTC`.\n  - `05:45 UTC` → `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:45 UTC`.\n  - `06:30 UTC` → `fold=1`, `utcoffset=-5h`, roundtrip `06:30 UTC`.\n- If a returned endpoint is wall-clock `01:30 America/New_York` but not equal to `datetime(2025,11,2,1,30, tzinfo=timezone(timedelta(hours=-4)))`, it likely represents `06:30 UTC` / `fold=1`, not `05:30 UTC` / `fold=0`.\n- Current `tests/test_slots.py` helpers include `UTC = timezone.utc`, `JST = timezone(timedelta(hours=9))`, `NY = timezone(timedelta(hours=-5))`, and functions `utc`, `jst`, `ny`.\n- Current visible `ledgerkit/slots.py` already converts `day_start`, `day_end`, and busy intervals to UTC with `astimezone(UTC)`, then clips/sorts/merges in UTC; the tail of the function, where gaps are converted back to local time, still needs inspection.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Original `ledgerkit/slots.py` and `tests/test_slots.py` created, tested, and committed as `0a201aa`.\n- Empirically reproduced the DST bug before fixing.\n- Rewrote `ledgerkit/slots.py` with UTC-normalized `free_slots` using `_is_naive` validation, UTC conversion, clip/sort/merge/gap logic in UTC.\n- Added `from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo` import to `tests/test_slots.py`.\n- Added two DST regression tests:\n  - `test_fall_back_day_full_window_survives_min_minutes`\n  - `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`\n- Corrected swapped test endpoints in `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` so the first gap ends at busy start and the second gap starts at busy end.\n- Ran CPython `astimezone` diagnostics confirming correct fold/utcoffset/roundtrip behavior for ambiguous times.\n- Read current `ledgerkit/slots.py` and `tests/test_slots.py` to begin debugging the remaining failure; no fix has been applied yet.\n\n### Active\n- `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` still fails: `first[1]` is `datetime(2025,11,2,1,30, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))` but does not equal `datetime(2025,11,2,1,30, tzinfo=timezone(timedelta(hours=-4)))`.\n- Need determine whether the returned `01:30` endpoint is `05:30 UTC` (`fold=0`, EDT) or `06:30 UTC` (`fold=1`, EST).\n- Suspected causes:\n  - `slots.py` converts UTC gap endpoints back to local time incorrectly.\n  - The test’s busy interval uses or implies `fold=1`, making the expected gap endpoints EST rather than EDT.\n- Last test run: 1 failed, 23 passed.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Inspect the full tail of `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/slots.py` after line 51 and the exact body of `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` in `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py`, including any `fold=` values on busy endpoints.\n2. Run a focused debug pass, such as `python3 -m pytest -q -k test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`, with prints for:\n   - `gaps[0][1].fold`\n   - `gaps[0][1].utcoffset()`\n   - `gaps[0][1].astimezone(timezone.utc)`\n   - busy start/end `.astimezone(timezone.utc)`\n   to identify whether the `01:30` endpoint is `05:30 UTC` or `06:30 UTC`.\n3. Fix the incorrect behavior:\n   - If `slots.py` is producing the wrong local conversion, correct the UTC-to-local conversion.\n   - If the test is using/expecting the wrong ambiguous fold, adjust the test to assert the intended instant, likely fixed `-4` for EDT if the busy interval is the first occurrence of the repeated hour.\n4. Re-run `python3 -m pytest -q` and confirm `24 passed`.\n5. `git add ledgerkit/slots.py tests/test_slots.py`, commit on `crew/1107-b2704c` (e.g. `Fix DST wall-clock arithmetic by doing interval math in UTC`), and do not push.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/slots.py`: contains `free_slots`; currently UTC-normalized through clipping/merging, but needs tail conversion/debugging to fix the failing ambiguous-time endpoint.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py`: 24 tests; failing `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`; includes `ZoneInfo` import and fixed-offset helpers.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing package module, unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_money.py`: existing tests, unchanged.","time":{"start":1794047158117,"end":1794047181271}}}
