{"type":"text","timestamp":1794047386525,"sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","part":{"id":"prt_1b58e2a2b001RQDkIJEnBefTLp","messageID":"msg_1b58c78ae001lRdvaSqTGJm0XV","sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the DST wall-clock arithmetic bug in `ledgerkit/slots.py` by normalizing interval math to UTC, add regression tests, make the slot tests pass, and commit on `crew/1107-b2704c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c`; branch: `crew/1107-b2704c`; Python: `3.12.3`.\n- Do not push or switch branches.\n- Original implementation and 22 tests were committed as `0a201aa`; the intended final state is a green slot-test suite, likely `24 passed` if all slot tests are collected.\n- `free_slots(busy, day_start, day_end, min_minutes=0)` must return sorted, timezone-aware gaps in `day_start`’s timezone, with clip/sort/merge/gap/duration math performed in UTC.\n- `busy` may be unsorted, overlapping, or use mixed offsets; zero-length busy intervals are ignored.\n- Required `ValueError` cases: naive datetimes, busy interval `end < start`, and `day_end <= day_start`.\n- Total free-time assertions must compare UTC durations: `sum(e.astimezone(timezone.utc) - s.astimezone(timezone.utc) for s, e in gaps)`.\n- Confirmed CPython behavior for `America/New_York` fall-back on `2025-11-02`:\n  - `05:30 UTC` → local `01:30`, `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:30 UTC`.\n  - `05:45 UTC` → local `01:45`, `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:45 UTC`.\n  - `06:30 UTC` → local `01:30`, `fold=1`, `utcoffset=-5h`, roundtrip `06:30 UTC`.\n- Latest `pytest` run: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_slots.py -x -q` reported `1 failed, 22 passed`; failure is `tests/test_slots.py::test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` at line `273`.\n- Debugging `free_slots` output shows the returned gaps are correct instants:\n  - Gap 1: `2025-11-02 00:00 America/New_York` to `2025-11-02 01:30 America/New_York`; UTC `04:00` to `05:30`; both `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`.\n  - Gap 2: `2025-11-02 01:45 America/New_York` to `2025-11-03 00:00 America/New_York`; UTC `05:45` to `2025-11-03 05:00`; start `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`; end `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-5h`.\n- The failing assertion compares a `ZoneInfo` datetime to a fixed-offset EDT datetime:\n  - Actual: `datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))`.\n  - Expected: `datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=timezone(timedelta(hours=-4)))`.\n  - Both convert to `2025-11-02 05:30:00+00:00`, both have `fold=0` and `utcoffset=-4h`, but direct `==` returned `False` in this environment.\n- Direct repro showed the same issue outside the test:\n  - `a = datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))`\n  - `b = datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=timezone(timedelta(hours=-4)))`\n  - `a.astimezone(UTC) == b.astimezone(UTC)` is true, `a - b == timedelta(0)` is true, but `a == b` printed `False`.\n- Therefore the current failure appears to be a mixed-`tzinfo` equality assertion issue in the test, not incorrect UTC-normalized interval math in `ledgerkit/slots.py`.\n- The fall-back day window `2025-11-02 00:00 America/New_York` to `2025-11-03 00:00 America/New_York` spans `25h` UTC. With a `15m` busy interval, the expected total free time is `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=45)`. If the test currently asserts `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=15)`, that assertion is wrong and should be corrected.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Original `ledgerkit/slots.py` and `tests/test_slots.py` created, tested, and committed as `0a201aa`.\n- Reproduced the DST wall-clock bug empirically before fixing.\n- Rewrote `ledgerkit/slots.py` to validate inputs and perform all interval math in UTC.\n- Added `from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo` to `tests/test_slots.py`.\n- Added DST regression tests:\n  - `test_fall_back_day_full_window_survives_min_minutes`\n  - `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`\n- Corrected swapped endpoint expectations in `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` so gap 1 ends at busy start and gap 2 starts at busy end.\n- Ran CPython diagnostics confirming expected `fold`, `utcoffset`, and UTC roundtrip behavior for ambiguous `America/New_York` times.\n- Ran the failing test and debugged `free_slots` output; confirmed the returned endpoints represent the intended UTC instants.\n- Identified that direct equality between `ZoneInfo('America/New_York')` and fixed `timezone(timedelta(hours=-4))` can be `False` despite identical UTC instants.\n\n### Active\n- `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` still fails at:\n  - `assert first[1] == datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=edt)`\n  - `tests/test_slots.py:273`\n- Need to adjust the test so it compares UTC instants, offsets, and/or fold values rather than relying on direct equality between different `tzinfo` types.\n- Need to verify and correct the total-free-time assertion for the fall-back day: expected `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=45)`, not `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=15)` if currently present.\n- Need to run the full slot test suite without `-x` to confirm no later tests fail.\n- No final commit has been made yet.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Edit `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py` in `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`:\n   - Replace direct mixed-`tzinfo` equality for `first[1]` with UTC-instant and offset checks, e.g. assert `first[1].astimezone(UTC) == datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=edt).astimezone(UTC)`, `first[1].utcoffset() == timedelta(hours=-4)`, and `first[1].fold == 0`.\n   - Apply the same robust comparison style to `second[0]` if the test asserts it directly.\n2. Check the total-free-time assertion in the same test:\n   - Compute it as `sum(e.astimezone(UTC) - s.astimezone(UTC) for s, e in gaps)`.\n   - Assert `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=45)` for the 25-hour fall-back day minus the 15-minute busy interval; fix it if it currently asserts `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=15)`.\n3. Run the full slot suite without stopping at the first failure:\n   - `python3 -m pytest tests/test_slots.py -q`\n   - Confirm all slot tests pass, ideally `24 passed` if that is the final collected count.\n4. If green, stage and commit only the changed work:\n   - `git add ledgerkit/slots.py tests/test_slots.py`\n   - Commit on `crew/1107-b2704c` with a message such as `Fix DST wall-clock arithmetic by doing interval math in UTC`.\n   - Do not push.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/slots.py`: contains `free_slots`; current UTC-normalized implementation appears correct based on debug output; likely needs no further logic change, but the uncommitted rewrite should be committed if final tests pass.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_slots.py`: contains the failing `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`; needs assertion changes to avoid mixed-`tzinfo` direct equality and to verify the correct total free time.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing package module, unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c/tests/test_money.py`: existing tests, unchanged.","time":{"start":1794047355435,"end":1794047386522}}}
