{"type":"text","timestamp":1794047447515,"sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","part":{"id":"prt_1b58f3e4a001R7vAqrRpMV7pJp","messageID":"msg_1b58edee0001JJsulBNW4S7P6z","sessionID":"ses_e4a838527ffe8oucTkjfNF4FOG","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Fix the DST wall-clock arithmetic bug in `ledgerkit/slots.py` by normalizing interval math to UTC, add regression tests, make the slot tests pass, and commit on `crew/1107-b2704c` without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-b2704c`; branch: `crew/1107-b2704c`; Python: `3.12.3`.\n- Do not push or switch branches.\n- Original implementation and 22 tests were committed as `0a201aa`; the final state should be a green slot-test suite plus a commit for the DST fix.\n- `free_slots(busy, day_start, day_end, min_minutes=0)` must return sorted, timezone-aware gaps in `day_start`’s timezone, with clip/sort/merge/gap/duration math performed in UTC.\n- `busy` may be unsorted, overlapping, or use mixed offsets; zero-length busy intervals are ignored.\n- Required `ValueError` cases: naive datetimes, busy interval `end < start`, and `day_end <= day_start`.\n- Confirmed CPython behavior for `America/New_York` fall-back on `2025-11-02`:\n  - `05:30 UTC` → local `01:30`, `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:30 UTC`.\n  - `05:45 UTC` → local `01:45`, `fold=0`, `utcoffset=-4h`, roundtrip `05:45 UTC`.\n  - `06:30 UTC` → local `01:30`, `fold=1`, `utcoffset=-5h`, roundtrip `06:30 UTC`.\n- Observed in this environment: direct `==` between `datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=ZoneInfo('America/New_York'))` and `datetime(2025, 11, 2, 1, 30, tzinfo=timezone(timedelta(hours=-4)))` returned `False`, while `astimezone(UTC)` values and `a - b` were equal. Test assertions were changed to compare UTC instants.\n- The fall-back day window `2025-11-02 00:00 America/New_York` to `2025-11-03 00:00 America/New_York` spans `25h` UTC. With a `15m` busy interval, total free time is `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=45)`.\n- Latest `pytest` run after UTC-instant assertion and total-duration fixes but before the `sum` start fix: `1 failed, 22 passed`; failure was `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'int' and 'datetime.timedelta'` at `tests/test_slots.py:276` because `sum()` over a generator of timedeltas starts from `int` `0`.\n- Current slot test collection appears to be `23` tests; after the `sum` fix the expected result is `23 passed`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Original `ledgerkit/slots.py` and `tests/test_slots.py` created, tested, and committed as `0a201aa`.\n- Reproduced the DST wall-clock bug empirically before fixing.\n- Rewrote `ledgerkit/slots.py` to validate inputs and perform all interval math in UTC.\n- Added `from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo` to `tests/test_slots.py`.\n- Added DST regression tests:\n  - `test_fall_back_day_full_window_survives_min_minutes`\n  - `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour`\n- Corrected swapped endpoint expectations in `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` so gap 1 ends at busy start and gap 2 starts at busy end.\n- Ran CPython diagnostics confirming expected `fold`, `utcoffset`, and UTC roundtrip behavior for ambiguous `America/New_York` times.\n- Ran the failing test and debugged `free_slots` output; confirmed the returned endpoints represent the intended UTC instants.\n- Changed mixed-`tzinfo` assertions in `test_busy_inside_repeated_fall_back_hour` to UTC-instant comparisons:\n  - `first[1].astimezone(UTC) == datetime(2025, 11, 2, 5, 30, tzinfo=UTC)`\n  - `second[0].astimezone(UTC) == datetime(2025, 11, 2, 5, 45, tzinfo=UTC)`\n- Changed the total-free-time assertion from `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=15)` to `timedelta(hours=24, minutes=45)`.\n- Ran `python3 -m pytest tests/test_slots.py -q`; it failed with `TypeError` in the `sum` expression.\n- Fixed the `sum` expression in `tests/test_slots.py` to use an explicit `timedelta(0)` start:\n  - `sum((end.astimezone